write(A,'Matter Brief.txt',f'''FICTIONAL TEACHING MATTER\n{CASE}\n\nMatter M-01. The client is considering an internal reorganisation of its service provider. The partner needs a supported explanation of the executed agreement and evidence questions before advising. A related tax team reviews the client’s September 2026 records. No real taxpayer identity, confidential client record or legally operative filing is included.\n\nThe firm’s information begins as scans, editable agreements, email instructions and transaction tables. The same sources return throughout the course.\nAll required work happens during class with Jotham. No homework is required.''')
contract=f'''FICTIONAL TEACHING AGREEMENT\nCONTRACT-01 v2\nStatus: executed teaching version. Effective date: 15 August 2026.\nCustomer: Victoria Services Ltd\nProvider: Equator Systems Ltd\nMatter: M-01\n\n1. Services\nThe provider will maintain the customer’s reporting application under the agreed service schedule.\n\n2. Support access\nOnly named support staff may access customer records. Access requires prior customer approval and is subject to confidentiality obligations.\n\n3. Change of control\n{CLAUSE}\n\n4. Fees\nThe customer pays the fees in the signed service schedule. No fee amount is supplied in this teaching agreement.\n\n5. Liability\nThe applicable liability position remains subject to the signed schedule and qualified review. This extract does not supply that schedule.\n\n6. Termination\nThe customer may terminate for an unremedied material breach after the notice procedure in the signed schedule.\n\n7. Confidentiality\nEach party must restrict use of confidential information to the agreed service purpose and permitted disclosures.\n\n8. Governing law\nThe teaching agreement states Ugandan law. Applicable requirements and advice require qualified review.\n\nThis is a fictional exercise, not a complete commercial agreement or legal advice.\n'''
write(A,'Contract - Executed v2.txt',contract)
write(A,'Contract - Superseded Draft v1.txt','''FICTIONAL TEACHING DRAFT\nCONTRACT-01 v1. Superseded and unsigned.\nClause 3: The customer must give prior written consent to any change of control of the provider.\nThe executed v2 adds the group-reorganisation exception. Do not treat v1 as the current agreement.''')
write(A,'Client Instruction.txt','''FICTIONAL CLIENT INSTRUCTION\nVictoria Services Ltd asks whether a proposed internal group reorganisation of Equator Systems Ltd needs consent under CONTRACT-01 v2.\nQuestion 1: What does the current clause require?\nQuestion 2: We have not supplied an ownership chart or confirmation of continued provider responsibility. What facts should we confirm?\nChanged-fact exercise: the provider instead transfers to a buyer outside its wholly owned group. Reassess the answer.\nDo not invent transaction facts.''')
write(A,'Contract Review Playbook.txt','''FICTIONAL FIRM PLAYBOOK v1\n1. Identify consent rules and preserve applicable exceptions.\n2. Retain a workable internal group-reorganisation exception, subject to continued responsibility.\n3. Consider notice for a qualifying internal reorganisation. The notice period and recipient require agreement.\n4. Named support access needs prior approval and confidentiality under clause 2.\n5. Obtain missing schedules before concluding on fees, liability or termination procedure.\n6. Every proposed amendment needs a rationale and partner review.\nThese are teaching preferences, not statements of mandatory law.''')
write(A,'Public Sources.txt','PUBLIC RESEARCH SOURCES\nReviewed 25 October 2026. Check current source and applicability before teaching.\n\n'+'\n'.join(k+': '+v for k,v in SOURCES.items())+'\n\nPublic case candidate: Goal Relief Development Organisation v Uganda Revenue Authority, Civil Appeal 50 of 2023, [2024] UGCommC 272. Verify the judgment itself before making any substantive claim. Access can fail. The course supplies no invented holding. Use the fictional attribution exercise if the public judgment is unavailable, and label it accordingly.')
