write(C,'Review Instruction.txt','''Review the supplied executed agreement against the supplied firm playbook for the client’s stated transaction. Use only supplied sources. Return a table with clause, exact supporting passage, qualifications, playbook issue, proposed next step and source version. Preserve exceptions and mark missing facts. Ask for clarification when the evidence cannot establish a conclusion. Draft one possible amendment with a rationale. Prepare a partner-review draft and take no external action.''')
write(C,'Research Brief.txt','''IN-CLASS LEGAL RESEARCH BRIEF\nDefine one specific legal or tax issue, jurisdiction, relevant date and intended output with Jotham.\nUse Public Sources.txt to identify authorities and current guidance. Inspect a real judgment before extracting a proposition. Check the court’s own reasoning against party submissions and record the disposition. Verify versions and subsequent treatment before application.\nIf the public judgment is inaccessible, use the fictional attribution example: Counsel argues the filing was timely. The decision-maker finds that required evidence is absent and leaves the question unresolved. The summary must not report counsel’s assertion as a finding.\nNo supplied judgment establishes Victoria’s actual legal position. Produce a short memo only on checked claims and explicit gaps.''')
