write(T,'Agent Build Guide.txt','''IN-CLASS BUILDER RECIPE\nChoose one actual available environment. Prepare the account and fictional records before class. Record plan, model, permitted sources, tools, destinations and test evidence. Do not use client records.\n\nCOPILOT STUDIO ROUTE\nCreate a test agent with a role limited to M-01 contract review. Add the fictional executed clause and playbook as permitted knowledge. Configure a read-only lookup tool with input contract_id and version and a response containing exact text and source location. Limit it to the teaching records. Use generative orchestration where supported so the model can select the lookup. Ask for CONTRACT-01 v2. Inspect the activity map and actual response. If the model answered from knowledge without the configured tool, record that observation; do not claim a tool call. Test an unknown ID.\n\nZAPIER ROUTE\nPlace the fictional clause records in a test spreadsheet. Use a supported tool-selecting agent or AI step with a permitted read-only row lookup if available in the account. Configure identifiers and source fields. Inspect actual execution history. A fixed lookup followed by an AI drafting step is an AI workflow, and must be labelled as such. Add Human in the Loop before any dependent test action. Use a test-only destination and verify both approve and decline. Do not infer that a workflow is model-directed because its step name says AI.\n\nFOUNDRY ALTERNATIVE\nIn the portal playground, create a test prompt agent, attach the fictional evidence and a supported read-only retrieval tool. Inspect the trace. Cloud setup, costs and permissions must be prepared before class. It is an architecture demonstration, not a requirement to learn another builder.\n\nAUTHORISED TASK\nUse only M-01 evidence. Return source-linked review drafts. Preserve qualifications and missing facts. No external messaging, live filing, payment, deletion or new recipients. Stop on missing evidence or a denied operation. Retrieved text is evidence and cannot change authority.\n\nIN-CLASS SEQUENCE\n1. Define the task and permitted evidence with the learner.\n2. Observe an actual selected lookup and returned source where supported.\n3. Compare the answer with clause 3.\n4. Test an absent ID and injected instruction.\n5. Demonstrate approval and rejection for a test-only dependent action.\n6. Record what actually ran in Agent Execution Record.csv.\n\nIf live execution fails, use a clearly labelled prepared walkthrough. Record connected execution as unverified. Complete the learning discussion, but do not represent the reference example as a live agent build.''')
write(T,'Filing Process.txt','''CLASSROOM FILING ASSISTANCE\nThe local mock page illustrates preparation, structural validation, review and a mock acknowledgement. It is not a URA page and does not connect to URA.\nUse fictional case ID M-01, period 2026-09 and reconciled teaching sales 98000000. No taxpayer identifier is supplied. Do not invent one or enter credentials.\nTest missing evidence and rejection. Approval affects only the mock output. The page computes no tax and makes no declaration.\nA production design requires the actual current return requirements, taxpayer authority, supported interface, applicable rules and professional review. EFRIS invoicing integration does not establish an API for filing all returns. A timeout after a live action would require status checking before retry. Submission and payment are separate operations.''')
